  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb — follows standard endings in every tense, no exceptions.",
    "Not reflexive: *callar* means to quiet or silence someone/something, or to keep quiet about something (*callar un secreto*, \"to keep a secret quiet\"). The reflexive form *callarse* (\"to fall silent / shut up\") is more common in everyday speech and is a separate verb file if needed.",
    "*El profesor calló a la clase con una mirada.* (\"The teacher silenced the class with a look.\")",
    "*Ella prefirió callar la verdad.* (\"She preferred to keep the truth quiet.\")",
    "Related: *callarse* (reflexive, \"to be/go quiet\"), *silencioso/a* (silent, adjective), *el silencio* (silence)."
  ],
